@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;isolation] ingress-bridge-boundaries
Only lilly-hostd runs this helper, inside its command cgroup, with argv it
derived itself: the accepted end of a connection whose peer is a socket the
Lilly BEAM created, and the guest TCP connection hostd dialled inside the
Lilly network namespace. Run as root it first drops to the service uid with
no supplementary groups and no_new_privs; it holds no capability, setuid bit
or other descriptor. Guest and Lilly bytes move only between those two
sockets through kernel pipes, never to stdout, stderr or a diagnostic.
Cancellation is hostd killing its cgroup.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] ingress-bridge-hegel-properties
Hegel properties MUST cover the command line against an independent oracle
and the per-direction byte accounting, while process fixtures cover exact
byte custody both ways, half-close ordering, Lilly's close ending the
bridge, guest loss, refusals and the privilege drop.
